{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.GbResidueSpectralSum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.GbResidueSpectralSum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Abs","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.BraneTower"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.fromCrystalData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.fromCrystalData","kind":"def","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L252-L268","doc":"Construct a `GBResidueSpectralSum` from explicit per-level\ndata.  The `mass` field is forced to the canonical decomposition\n`|descended| + Σ_ℓ residue ℓ`, and `spectral_decomposition`\nholds by `rfl`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.spectral_decomposition_extended","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.spectral_decomposition_extended","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L223-L232","doc":"The spectral sum may be taken over the extended residue on the initial\nsegment `Fin levelBound` without change — the extension agrees with\n`residue` everywhere it is defined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.spectral_sum_finite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.spectral_sum_finite","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L173-L221","doc":"**Finiteness of the spectral sum.** The extended residue vanishes at every\nlevel at or above the confinement bound, so the sum has finitely many\nnon-zero terms.\n\n## Restated 2026-09-04 (bean `qou-tmmt`) — the previous statement was vacuous\n\nIt read\n\n    ∃ N, ∀ ℓ ≥ N, ∀ (h : ℓ < S.levelBound),\n      S.residue ⟨ℓ, h⟩ = 0 ∨ ℓ < S.levelBound\n\nand was proved by `exact Or.inr h` — **the right disjunct is the hypothesis\n`h` itself**. So it held for every `S` and every `residue` whatsoever, with\nany `N` at all, and asserted nothing about vanishing or finiteness. Its own\ndocstring recorded the cause: the block's actual claim,\n`∃ N, ∀ ℓ ≥ N, residueAtRoot ℓ ζ q = 0`, was described as becoming \"a\ntautology in the class-based formulation\", and the free disjunct was added\nto make it provable rather than the statement being repaired.\n\nIt is not a tautology — it is a statement about a function on `ℕ`, and\n`residue : Fin levelBound → R` is not one. With the zero-extension above,\nthe block's original claim goes through directly, and the extension is what\nthe prose meant by \"strata above this give zero contribution\".\n\n## What this does NOT establish\n\nThe vanishing proved here is of the **canonical zero-extension**, which is\nwhat makes finiteness statable at all. It is not the conjectural claim, and\nthe library twin `QOU.BraidKnot.spectral_sum_finite` in\n`lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBResidueSpectralSum.lean` states that correctly: the\nsubstantive content of `conj:gs-spectral-sum-finite` is that `levelBound`\n*truly equals* the confinement level `ℓ(K, q₀)` of the underlying braid, so\nthat any **analytic** extension of `residue` to `ℕ` vanishes above the\ncutoff. Nothing here bears on that. Extending by zero and then observing\nthat the extension is zero would be circular if offered as evidence for it.\n\nNote also that the library twin carries the *same declaration name* in the\nsame namespace while proving a different statement — there,\n`card (univ : Finset (Fin levelBound)) = levelBound`, the algebraic\nfiniteness. A content-block sibling is outside the Lake glob so the two do\nnot collide at build time, but `gs-spectral-sum-finite.ts` resolves its\n`lean.ref` to the library one, not to this. Recorded in bean `qou-tmmt`.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] `prop:confinement-level-unique`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:gs-spectral-sum-finite","label":"conj:gs-spectral-sum-finite","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gs-spectral-sum-finite.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.residueAtLevel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.residueAtLevel","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L166-L171","doc":"The residue extended to **every** level, by zero above the confinement\nbound. This is the object the finiteness claim is about: `residue` alone is\na function on `Fin levelBound`, so \"vanishes above the bound\" cannot even be\nstated for it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.classical_limit_descended","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.classical_limit_descended","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L154-L164","doc":"Classical limit: when every cyclotomic residue vanishes (in the\n`q = 1` commutative limit all roots of unity coincide at `1` and\nthe cyclotomic projections collapse), the mass reduces to the\ndescended Markov trace.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] `prop:categorical-mass-markov`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gradedMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gradedMarkovTrace","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L149-L152","doc":"Convenience accessor: the graded trace at level `ℓ`.  Replaces\nthe previous `opaque gradedMarkovTrace ℓ q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.residueAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.residueAt","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L144-L147","doc":"Convenience accessor: the residue at level `ℓ` for a spectral-sum\ninstance.  Replaces the previous `opaque residueAtRoot ℓ ζ q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.spectral_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.spectral_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L141-L141","doc":"Consistency: the mass is the descended term plus the sum of residues over\nfiltration levels.  This is the content of `prop:gb-residue-spectral-sum`, and\nthe **only** `Prop` field of the class.\n\nNote what it does and does not buy.  It constrains `mass` — but `mass` is\nitself a free field, so any tuple inhabits the class: choose the six data\nfields freely, set `mass := |descended| + ∑ residue ℓ`, and discharge this by\n`rfl`.  So it fixes one field relative to the others rather than constraining\nanything outside the class. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:gs-spectral-decomposition-existence","label":"conj:gs-spectral-decomposition-existence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gs-spectral-decomposition-existence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.mass","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L131-L131","doc":"The spectral sum:\n`𝔪 = |descended| + Σ_ℓ residue ℓ`.\n\nEquivalent to the previous statement\n`mass = |descended| + Σ_ℓ residueAtRoot ℓ.val (roots ℓ) q`,\nwith `residue ℓ` standing in for the unfolded\n`residueAtRoot ℓ.val (roots ℓ) q` term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.residue","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L123-L123","doc":"The residue value at level `ℓ`, **supplied freely by the instance**.\n\n*Intended* meaning, per `prop:residue-at-root`: the cyclotomic projection of\n`Φ_q · gradedTrace ℓ` in the Habiro completion.  **That is not encoded here** —\nin particular nothing relates `residue` to `gradedTrace`, despite the prose,\nso the two are independent data.  Encoding it needs the Habiro-ring\ninfrastructure the module header defers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.gradedTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.gradedTrace","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L115-L115","doc":"The graded trace value at level `ℓ`, **supplied freely by the instance**.\n\n*Intended* meaning, per `prop:graded-markov-trace-from-gs-filtration`: the\nvalue of `tr_M` descended to `J^ℓ / J^{ℓ+1}`.  **That is not encoded here** —\nno field relates this to `tr_M`, to the filtration, or to `descended`, so an\ninstance may supply any function at all.  Encoding it needs the\nGS-filtration infrastructure the module header defers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.roots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.roots","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L107-L107","doc":"The roots of unity indexed by filtration level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.q","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L105-L105","doc":"The substrate parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.levelBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.levelBound","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L103-L103","doc":"The confinement-level cutoff `ℓ(K, q)`.  Strata above this\ngive zero contribution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.descended","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.descended","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L100-L100","doc":"The descended (E⁰) Markov trace of the braid word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBResidueSpectralSum","kind":"class","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L79-L142","doc":"**GB residue spectral sum.**\n\nThe mass of a closed braid `K` with Hecke normal form `T_w` is\n\n  𝔪(K) = |tr_M(T_w)| + Σ_{ℓ=0}^{levelBound-1} Res_{q→ζ_ℓ}(Φ_q · tr_{M,ℓ})(T_w)\n\nThis is the E∞ page of the residue spectral sequence of the\nGröbner–Shirshov–filtered Hecke algebra `H_n(q)`, evaluated on\n`T_w`.\n\nEach instance carries:\n  * `descended` — the descended (E⁰) Markov trace.\n  * `levelBound` — the confinement level cutoff.\n  * `gradedTrace ℓ` — the induced trace on `J^ℓ / J^{ℓ+1}`,\n    per `prop:graded-markov-trace-from-gs-filtration`.\n    Replaces the previous `opaque gradedMarkovTrace`.\n  * `residue ℓ` — the cyclotomic residue\n    `Res_{q→ζ_ℓ}(Φ_q · tr_{M,ℓ})`, per `prop:residue-at-root`.\n    Replaces the previous `opaque residueAtRoot`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnity.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnity.value","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L77-L77","doc":"The coordinate of `ζ_ℓ` in the ambient ring `R`. At `R := ℝ` this is the\nreal part; a full Mathlib treatment would take `R := ℂ`. Abstracting `R`\nis how the library states it, and it says the same thing without pinning\nthe ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnity.n_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnity.n_pos","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnity.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnity.n","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RootOfUnity","kind":"structure","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-residue-spectral-sum.lean#L67-L77","doc":"A root of unity `ζ_ℓ` at which the `ℓ`-th knot-operator energy\n`E_ℓ(q)` vanishes. In the formal development each `ζ_ℓ` is a\nprimitive `n_ℓ`-th root of unity for some `n_ℓ ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}